      "content": "The idea of using the inherent value of historical assets as a silent signal is compelling. It allows for a sort of prestige that is felt rather than declared.\n\nI have been looking into acquiring certain uncatalogued manuscripts from the late Valerian period—items that are currently held in private collections. If I were to acquire these, would you agree that it would serve as a powerful, wordless way to signal my identity to those who truly know the history? And how might I utilize such an acquisition to test the loyalty of a prospective advisor without me having to explicitly state who I am?",
